WEBVTT

00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:27.778
Oh!

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:50.342
Hey, guys. Welcome to my parents'
40th anniversary party.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.010
I'm bored. Let's drink.

00:00:57.349 --> 00:00:59.309
Wow, what a turnout.

00:00:59.393 --> 00:01:01.937
It's great to see so many happy smiles,

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.564
most of them on Mouth Mutant.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.525
Hey-o!

00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:09.570
But let me just say, for 40 years,

00:01:09.695 --> 00:01:12.906
my beautiful wife Munda
has been by my side,

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:16.785
even that year my side mutated
into some kind of venomous radish.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:20.664
And, Morris, I fell in love
with your honesty and humility.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.208
And those things never mutated.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:25.961
Aw!

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.754
Aw!

00:01:27.838 --> 00:01:30.924
Now, if you'll direct your attention
to this moldy shower curtain,

00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:33.844
I've prepared a video tribute
to the happy couple.

00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:38.765
In their 40 years together,

00:01:39.141 --> 00:01:41.643
my parents have been through so much.

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.562
Well, not that much, actually,

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:46.732
since mutants weren't allowed
to leave the sewers until last year.

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:49.610
Like anyone wants to leave the sewer.
Am I right?

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:52.738
Shush, Morris.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.615
So, how did it all begin?

00:01:54.698 --> 00:01:57.409
The unlikely lovebirds
met at Brown University.

00:01:57.781 --> 00:02:00.533
She, a brilliant exolinguistics major,

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.789
he, a laid-back sewer surfer

00:02:02.915 --> 00:02:05.584
who didn't even know
the meaning of "exolinguistics."

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.044
I still have no idea.

00:02:09.338 --> 00:02:11.507
I've been telling you for 40 years,

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.218
it's the study of alien languages.

00:02:14.484 --> 00:02:15.611
Why can't you listen?

00:02:15.694 --> 00:02:16.903
Oh, sugar lump,

00:02:16.987 --> 00:02:20.073
I hear you when you actually say
something important.

00:02:20.198 --> 00:02:22.367
But sometimes opposites attract,

00:02:22.451 --> 00:02:25.621
and like the fairy tale
of face mutant and butt mutant,

00:02:25.704 --> 00:02:29.499
the love of Munda and Morris
has grown stronger every day.

00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:31.543
"Something important"?

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:33.795
Exolinguistics was my passion.

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:37.758
Until I gave it up to go into
the lucrative pot-roast-making field.

00:02:37.841 --> 00:02:39.217
Pot-roast-burning.

00:02:39.301 --> 00:02:41.595
I never got why you studied
that alien junk anyway.

00:02:41.762 --> 00:02:44.139
We can't even see the stars
down here in the sewer.

00:02:44.222 --> 00:02:45.474
Why can't you accept that?

00:02:45.682 --> 00:02:48.560
I did accept it. For 40 years!

00:02:48.644 --> 00:02:50.687
But now we're free to go up there.

00:02:50.771 --> 00:02:53.690
I could be in space
seeing things I've only dreamed about,

00:02:53.774 --> 00:02:55.317
if it weren't for you!

00:02:55.776 --> 00:02:56.818
Uh...

00:02:56.902 --> 00:02:59.237
Okay, everybody, thanks for coming.

00:02:59.321 --> 00:03:00.864
I had dreams, too!

00:03:01.156 --> 00:03:06.244
I was going to surf the world's sewers,
but I happily gave it up for you. Happily!

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.497
I just want a little more out of life.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.168
But no, you don't want to go into space
because you're too afraid.

00:03:13.251 --> 00:03:16.046
You bet I'm afraid. You want to go? Go!

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:18.256
Get your head knocked off by a meteorite.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.467
Okay, take a deep breath.

00:03:20.676 --> 00:03:23.887
You're having a little lovers' quarrel,
but I'm sure you'll work everything...

00:03:25.097 --> 00:03:26.598
Divorce is final.

00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:32.187
Don't worry.
I'm only going to stay with you

00:03:32.271 --> 00:03:34.523
until a vacancy opens up on this floor.

00:03:34.856 --> 00:03:37.609
You know, the rents
are a lot more reasonable in Peru.

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.778
Come on, Leela, let's go out.

00:03:39.861 --> 00:03:42.281
After 40 years, I want to see the world.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:47.119
What the heck? You want to go out?
Let's really go out.

00:04:05.512 --> 00:04:07.097
Dance, slave, dance.

00:04:26.049 --> 00:04:29.302
Well, I lost two straight hands
to the Borax Kid.

00:04:29.428 --> 00:04:33.348
I don't really have any use for these,
but you can't have them back. Ladies.

00:04:33.974 --> 00:04:37.018
Imagine. Me, a girl from the sewer

00:04:37.102 --> 00:04:40.021
meeting a man made entirely of detergent.

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:42.524
And look over there!

00:04:42.733 --> 00:04:45.777
It's Zapp Brannigan,
the famous space captain.

00:04:46.027 --> 00:04:47.654
Hey, I have an idea.

00:04:47.738 --> 00:04:50.073
Let's look in a different direction
at something else.

00:04:50.157 --> 00:04:51.366
You go ahead, dear.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:54.828
I wonder what Captain Brannigan's doing
with those Carcarons.

00:04:55.037 --> 00:04:57.622
Now, regarding this peace treaty,
Admiral Chu.

00:04:57.873 --> 00:04:59.916
That's a napkin dispenser, sir.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.210
This is the universal translator.

00:05:02.377 --> 00:05:03.587
Whatever.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.340
Now, Admiral, in exchange
for your promise not to attack us,

00:05:07.424 --> 00:05:11.928
we will grant you exclusive fishing rights
in Supernova Scotia.

00:05:18.602 --> 00:05:20.437
Well, okay.

00:05:20.604 --> 00:05:23.190
Excellent.
We'll meet aboard my ship in one month

00:05:23.273 --> 00:05:25.567
to sign the Treaty of Table Seven.

00:05:27.444 --> 00:05:28.904
Table Seven?

00:05:30.155 --> 00:05:33.075
Now, watch, Kif,
as I score a diplomatic coupe

00:05:33.158 --> 00:05:36.078
by congratulating the Admiral
in his native tongue.

00:05:36.286 --> 00:05:40.248
Last time you tried that,
the Mexican restaurant declared war on us.

00:05:40.332 --> 00:05:42.417
I beg you, just use the translator.

00:05:42.626 --> 00:05:44.795
Kif, just trust me for once.

00:05:47.339 --> 00:05:49.841
I'd like to spank your sister
with a slice of bologna.

00:05:50.092 --> 00:05:51.593
Oops!

00:05:58.308 --> 00:05:59.309
Oh...

00:05:59.393 --> 00:06:02.187
It's the Battle of Paco's Tacos
all over again.

00:06:06.483 --> 00:06:07.984
Mom, what are you doing?

00:06:08.068 --> 00:06:09.569
What I was trained to do.

00:06:16.618 --> 00:06:17.911
What did you say to them?

00:06:17.994 --> 00:06:21.915
Just that Captain Brannigan
confused the word for "congratulations"

00:06:21.998 --> 00:06:24.376
with the word
for "spank your sister with bologna."

00:06:24.626 --> 00:06:26.294
Nicely squawked, madam.

00:06:26.503 --> 00:06:28.839
Leela, you never told me you had a mother.

00:06:28.922 --> 00:06:32.050
I insist you stay
for a courtesy thank you drink.

00:06:35.887 --> 00:06:36.972
Mmm!

00:06:37.055 --> 00:06:39.516
Good barium shots. Expensive, though.

00:06:39.599 --> 00:06:42.477
We can put it on the corporate card,
as long as we discuss business.

00:06:43.603 --> 00:06:45.772
So, uh, yesterday, huh?

00:06:45.856 --> 00:06:48.108
That business happened, right?

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:49.860
Somebody?

00:06:49.943 --> 00:06:51.528
I'll just pay for it.

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:54.364
Well, we should get going.
You guys see where my mom went?

00:06:54.448 --> 00:06:56.032
I don't know where most of her is,

00:06:56.116 --> 00:06:57.659
but her tongue's in Zapp's mouth.

00:07:02.247 --> 00:07:03.290
Whoo!

00:07:03.373 --> 00:07:04.541
Nasty.

00:07:29.149 --> 00:07:32.235
Mom, are you okay?
Did Zapp take advantage of you?

00:07:32.319 --> 00:07:34.613
Show me where he touched you
on this dried-apple doll.

00:07:34.696 --> 00:07:38.075
Don't be silly.
Zapp's a perfect gentleman.

00:07:38.158 --> 00:07:40.077
And so handsome.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.579
Did you know he wears a velour man-skirt?

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:46.708
Mom, I hate to break it to you,
but Zapp's a jerk.

00:07:46.792 --> 00:07:48.168
The truth is,

00:07:48.251 --> 00:07:50.587
I once slept with him. A few times.

00:07:50.837 --> 00:07:53.632
I know. He showed me
the commemorative painting.

00:07:53.757 --> 00:07:56.551
- What?
- Look, sweetie, I get it.

00:07:56.635 --> 00:07:59.721
You're jealous because Zapp
likes me now and not you.

00:07:59.846 --> 00:08:02.432
But don't worry, this isn't a competition.

00:08:02.516 --> 00:08:04.309
Although he did say I'm a better kisser.

00:08:04.559 --> 00:08:06.395
I am not jealous.

00:08:06.478 --> 00:08:08.188
Also... Yuck!

00:08:10.524 --> 00:08:13.693
Zapp doesn't care about my mom.
He's just doing this to get to me.

00:08:13.902 --> 00:08:15.028
Don't worry, Leela.

00:08:15.112 --> 00:08:16.738
Your mom won't see Zapp much.

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:18.115
He's in space all the time.

00:08:20.033 --> 00:08:23.537
Guess what, honey?
Zapp hired me as his personal translator.

00:08:23.620 --> 00:08:25.997
I'll be with him all the time. In space.

00:08:26.164 --> 00:08:29.167
- What? But...
- I've never been so happy!

00:08:29.251 --> 00:08:31.169
Hang on, Mom. I have another call.

00:08:39.386 --> 00:08:40.595
Thank you for coming.

00:08:40.679 --> 00:08:43.932
You know, without your mother,
the sewer's a dank and dismal place.

00:08:44.224 --> 00:08:46.309
Dad, we need to talk.

00:08:46.393 --> 00:08:47.477
Mom is...

00:08:47.561 --> 00:08:49.730
Well, she's seeing someone else.

00:08:49.896 --> 00:08:51.523
Who is it, Mouth Mutant?

00:08:51.606 --> 00:08:54.067
I ought to punch him
right in his big mouth.

00:08:54.151 --> 00:08:55.652
And then in all his smaller mouths!

00:08:55.736 --> 00:08:56.862
No, no, listen.

00:08:57.154 --> 00:08:59.072
It's time to get on with your life.

00:08:59.197 --> 00:09:01.324
But she was my life.

00:09:01.408 --> 00:09:02.451
Aw!

00:09:05.454 --> 00:09:06.538
What?

00:09:06.621 --> 00:09:08.874
Hey, what about your lifelong dream?

00:09:08.957 --> 00:09:11.585
Didn't you always want to surf
the world's greatest sewers?

00:09:11.668 --> 00:09:14.504
Yeah, and Fry and Bender can go with you.

00:09:14.755 --> 00:09:16.381
You can teach them how to surf,

00:09:16.465 --> 00:09:18.383
and they can make sure you don't...

00:09:22.087 --> 00:09:24.589
I don't know.
Would you come, too, sweetie?

00:09:24.673 --> 00:09:28.301
I can't. I have to keep an eye on Mom
to make sure she and Zapp don't...

00:09:31.722 --> 00:09:33.306
Yee-haw!

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:35.642
You know what?
I'm going to give it a shot.

00:09:35.726 --> 00:09:39.438
Let's go surf the great sewer waves
of the world!

00:10:46.171 --> 00:10:47.255
Where have you been?

00:10:47.339 --> 00:10:48.965
What? It's 2:00 in the afternoon.

00:10:49.257 --> 00:10:52.135
Several days later.
Look, enough is enough.

00:10:52.219 --> 00:10:55.138
Zapp is a jerk.
I insist you break up with him.

00:10:55.389 --> 00:10:57.474
Why can't you just let me be happy?

00:10:57.557 --> 00:11:00.936
After all these years,
I'm going places I've never been,

00:11:01.019 --> 00:11:02.145
and having sex there.

00:11:02.521 --> 00:11:04.147
You're too old to be happy.

00:11:04.231 --> 00:11:06.775
I'm not too old to enjoy
hot sex with Zapp.

00:11:06.858 --> 00:11:08.151
Ugh!

00:11:08.402 --> 00:11:09.945
Sex with Zapp!

00:11:10.028 --> 00:11:11.780
Sex with Zapp! Sex with Zapp!

00:11:11.905 --> 00:11:13.657
No, no!

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:17.119
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I don't think I can live here anymore.

00:11:17.202 --> 00:11:19.871
I'll be back for my things at 8:00 sharp.

00:11:22.374 --> 00:11:23.709
Sex with Zapp!

00:11:27.504 --> 00:11:30.257
- This one is for the E. coli.
- Ow!

00:11:30.507 --> 00:11:33.927
- And this one's for the leprechaunorrhea.
- Hiddly-dee!

00:11:34.177 --> 00:11:37.389
I don't care how many diseases Fry has.
It was worth it.

00:11:37.681 --> 00:11:40.434
Right on, brah! I feel free as a bum.

00:11:40.684 --> 00:11:42.477
How can you be so calm, Dad?

00:11:42.561 --> 00:11:43.687
The woman you love is out there

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:46.523
having the time of her life
with Zapp Brannigan,

00:11:46.606 --> 00:11:48.483
and you're not doing anything to stop it.

00:11:48.567 --> 00:11:50.652
Surfing helped me chill out, honey.

00:11:50.736 --> 00:11:54.573
When you're down there riding the waves,
the wind ripening in your face,

00:11:54.656 --> 00:11:57.075
everything just makes sense, dude.

00:11:57.534 --> 00:11:59.077
You mind if I call you dude, princess?

00:11:59.411 --> 00:12:02.039
Look, I don't want
to put a rat in your face-cage,

00:12:02.122 --> 00:12:04.082
or whatever you kids say nowadays,

00:12:04.166 --> 00:12:07.919
but Zapp's using Mom to get to me,
and I'm going to prove it!

00:12:10.672 --> 00:12:14.676
Kif, I'm bored. What say you go out
on the wing and pretend you're a gremlin?

00:12:16.678 --> 00:12:20.265
Well, if it isn't
my second favorite Turanga girl.

00:12:20.432 --> 00:12:22.392
Hi, Zapp. I was wondering if you'd like

00:12:22.476 --> 00:12:24.478
to have dinner tonight
with me and my mom.

00:12:24.561 --> 00:12:27.022
You know,
to celebrate your genuine love for her.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:28.273
Sounds good.

00:12:28.357 --> 00:12:31.610
And don't forget
my genuine love for Parmezian cheese.

00:12:31.693 --> 00:12:35.739
Shall we say about, mmm, 7:58? Precisely?

00:12:41.119 --> 00:12:42.663
Nice to see you, Zapp.

00:12:42.871 --> 00:12:45.666
Well, nice to see
a surprising amount of you, too, Leela.

00:12:45.749 --> 00:12:46.875
Is Munda here?

00:12:46.958 --> 00:12:49.294
Mommy's not home, big boy.

00:12:49.378 --> 00:12:51.672
We both know you're just using her
to get to me.

00:12:51.755 --> 00:12:56.009
So let's do it
right here by the front door at 7:59.

00:13:00.347 --> 00:13:03.225
Leela, does your mother know
you're using her pole?

00:13:04.476 --> 00:13:05.727
Come on, I'm all yours!

00:13:05.811 --> 00:13:08.313
Have your way with me
for the next 30 seconds.

00:13:08.563 --> 00:13:10.524
That would be more than enough time,

00:13:10.607 --> 00:13:12.150
but I can't. I love Munda.

00:13:12.651 --> 00:13:15.779
I love everything about her,
her laugh, her maturity,

00:13:15.862 --> 00:13:19.366
the cold, lifeless touch
of her tentacle on my body.

00:13:19.449 --> 00:13:22.536
She is one juicy calamari.

00:13:22.619 --> 00:13:25.372
Oh, Zapp, I love you, too.

00:13:26.581 --> 00:13:29.668
Oh, squiddums!
I've been thinking about this for a while,

00:13:29.751 --> 00:13:33.088
and, well, here in front
of your half-naked daughter

00:13:33.171 --> 00:13:35.007
seems like the perfect time.

00:13:35.382 --> 00:13:38.343
Darling, will I marry you?

00:13:38.552 --> 00:13:40.470
Of course, I'll marry you, Zapp.

00:13:44.558 --> 00:13:48.020
I, uh, think a motel room
might be in order.

00:13:48.103 --> 00:13:49.855
Leela, here's $40.

00:13:49.938 --> 00:13:53.692
Mom, don't do this.
Zapp is a selfish, womanizing idiot.

00:13:54.026 --> 00:13:56.069
There's no need to call me names, Leela.

00:13:56.153 --> 00:13:58.405
Just call me, "Daddy."

00:14:06.371 --> 00:14:08.290
Mom, if you try to marry Zapp,

00:14:08.373 --> 00:14:12.794
I will shove you into a filthy nursing
home so fast you won't know what hit you.

00:14:13.462 --> 00:14:15.339
Probably, it'll be a filthy nurse.

00:14:15.422 --> 00:14:18.925
Leela, you're my daughter
and I love you, but cram it!

00:14:19.343 --> 00:14:20.552
Is this a bad time?

00:14:20.635 --> 00:14:22.512
I was riding the El Torito
dinner backwash,

00:14:22.596 --> 00:14:23.805
and I thought I'd pop in.

00:14:23.889 --> 00:14:25.057
Oh, thank God you're here.

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:28.435
If we don't do something,
Mom's going to marry Zapp Brannigan.

00:14:28.602 --> 00:14:30.729
So? He seems like a nice kahuna.

00:14:30.812 --> 00:14:33.190
Dad, stop being so mellow.

00:14:33.273 --> 00:14:35.233
Leela, honey, chill out.

00:14:35.484 --> 00:14:37.569
You got to take the good with the gnarly.

00:14:37.653 --> 00:14:40.822
Speaking of which, time for me
to shoot the IHOP dessert curl.

00:14:42.032 --> 00:14:43.075
Ugh!

00:14:49.581 --> 00:14:52.459
Aw! You sure you won't come
to your mom's wedding?

00:14:52.542 --> 00:14:54.336
There'll be chicken or fish, circle one.

00:14:54.419 --> 00:14:57.089
I can't.
Not when I believe with all my heart

00:14:57.172 --> 00:14:58.715
that this marriage is a mistake.

00:14:58.965 --> 00:15:01.635
I know you're upset
that your parents broke up.

00:15:01.718 --> 00:15:04.429
But what if Zapp
really does make Munda happy?

00:15:04.805 --> 00:15:06.765
What if they're meant to be together?

00:15:07.015 --> 00:15:09.935
Fry, that's just so...
I can't even believe...

00:15:10.018 --> 00:15:12.104
You are so totally...

00:15:12.187 --> 00:15:14.106
Right. You're right.

00:15:14.314 --> 00:15:18.944
I am? Huh! Maybe Zapp isn't the only one
who's marriage material.

00:15:20.445 --> 00:15:21.697
You're getting there.

00:15:36.545 --> 00:15:37.713
Leela?

00:15:37.796 --> 00:15:39.339
You look beautiful, Mom.

00:15:39.423 --> 00:15:43.385
Really? I'm not showing too much sucker
for a lady my age?

00:15:43.635 --> 00:15:46.805
Just the right amount.
You'll make a lovely bride.

00:15:47.222 --> 00:15:50.767
Oh, Mom, I'm sorry
I've been so horrible to you.

00:15:51.393 --> 00:15:54.938
Oh, you weren't so horrible.
Just enough to show you care.

00:16:11.496 --> 00:16:12.914
At ease, darling.

00:16:12.998 --> 00:16:15.459
Honored guests and Kif,

00:16:15.542 --> 00:16:20.339
one of a captain's many superpowers
is the ability to conduct marriage.

00:16:20.422 --> 00:16:23.842
So I will now join myself
in holy macaroni.

00:16:23.925 --> 00:16:27.220
Kif, raise the ceremonial mirror.

00:16:27.554 --> 00:16:29.890
Zapp, you magnificent bastard,

00:16:29.973 --> 00:16:32.976
do you take Munda to be your lawful...

00:16:34.186 --> 00:16:35.645
Alien ships approaching, sir.

00:16:38.774 --> 00:16:40.400
It's the Carcarons!

00:16:40.776 --> 00:16:44.404
Oh, meatballs. I forgot they were coming
to sign the peace treaty today.

00:16:44.696 --> 00:16:45.864
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:16:45.947 --> 00:16:49.409
my blushing translator and I
have business to tend to.

00:16:49.493 --> 00:16:54.164
In the meantime, enjoy the comic stylings
of Nixon and Agnew.

00:16:57.876 --> 00:16:59.294
Oh, Mr. Agnew?

00:17:02.422 --> 00:17:05.425
Munda, tell the Admiral
that by signing this peace treaty,

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:07.678
we will achieve harmony
between our worlds.

00:17:08.178 --> 00:17:10.472
Zapp, honey, this is the wrong document.

00:17:10.555 --> 00:17:13.725
It's not a peace treaty.
It says they're declaring war on us.

00:17:13.892 --> 00:17:15.310
Brilliant, isn't I?

00:17:15.394 --> 00:17:16.770
The moment they sign,

00:17:16.853 --> 00:17:22.359
we destroy their fleet in one glorious
burst of "self-defense."

00:17:22.442 --> 00:17:23.735
Up high, Mrs. Brannigan.

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:27.489
Don't leave me hanging, Mrs. Brannigan.

00:17:27.739 --> 00:17:31.034
I come from the sewer, but that is low.

00:17:31.118 --> 00:17:33.245
I'm not going to translate your lies.

00:17:33.370 --> 00:17:36.415
Munda, dear, as your captain
and soon-to-be husband,

00:17:36.498 --> 00:17:37.958
I gave you an order.

00:17:38.041 --> 00:17:41.753
Now, let's tell these vicious lies
and get back to our sacred vows.

00:17:41.837 --> 00:17:45.090
There's not going to be any wedding.
I don't want your fancy ring.

00:17:45.799 --> 00:17:47.175
Careful! That's glass!

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:50.721
Leela was right.
You're a lousy man and a lousy captain.

00:17:50.804 --> 00:17:53.724
And I'm going
to tell our Carcaron friends the truth.

00:17:55.517 --> 00:17:58.562
Zapp... Lying sack of...

00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:08.655
Well, this is awkward.
Our Carcaron friends declared war.

00:18:08.739 --> 00:18:11.408
Then, once again,
my lies have been proven true.

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:16.830
We're under attack and the wedding's off.

00:18:16.913 --> 00:18:18.915
Kif, return fire and the cake.

00:18:20.083 --> 00:18:22.878
Our weapons are disabled,
and you can't return ice cream cakes!

00:18:22.961 --> 00:18:24.004
We're doomed!

00:18:27.966 --> 00:18:29.509
Stop the wedding!

00:18:29.593 --> 00:18:30.635
- Who is that?
- Morris?

00:18:30.927 --> 00:18:33.388
I'm not giving up the love of my life
without a fight.

00:18:34.598 --> 00:18:36.266
Do I know you?

00:18:37.434 --> 00:18:40.479
Dad? I thought you were all Zen
with Mom getting remarried.

00:18:40.687 --> 00:18:44.024
I was at first.
But then I conquered my inner peace.

00:18:44.107 --> 00:18:47.235
If you care about something,
you've got to take action.

00:18:47.319 --> 00:18:49.321
Harsh, violent action!

00:18:54.993 --> 00:18:56.370
Kif, get us out of here.

00:18:57.621 --> 00:19:00.332
Navigation is out. We're sitting ducks.

00:19:00.582 --> 00:19:02.292
Is there an auxiliary control system?

00:19:02.376 --> 00:19:04.044
Yes, outside on the hull.

00:19:04.127 --> 00:19:06.171
But there are 20 separate control keys.

00:19:06.296 --> 00:19:09.299
No one could work them well enough
to ride out these energy waves.

00:19:09.383 --> 00:19:10.717
No one?

00:19:13.095 --> 00:19:14.888
It's time to hang 20!

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.767
Morris! What are you doing?

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:22.896
Hold on to your coconuts.
We're going for the ride of a lifetime!

00:19:28.735 --> 00:19:31.571
But I thought
you were terrified of outer space.

00:19:31.697 --> 00:19:33.490
I was, but then it hit me.

00:19:33.573 --> 00:19:35.075
If heaven's above us,

00:19:35.158 --> 00:19:39.329
then the whole universe
is just God's glorious sewer.

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:52.217
Hang on, sweetie!

00:19:53.677 --> 00:19:55.554
What do we do? Who do we blame?

00:19:55.637 --> 00:19:58.306
We don't blame anyone. We make peace.

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.058
One word can end this.

00:20:00.225 --> 00:20:03.562
- Then say it.
- No, you say it.

00:20:22.289 --> 00:20:26.043
This actual peace treaty
is hereby enacted.

00:20:26.126 --> 00:20:28.420
Agnew, give it your stamp of approval.

00:20:33.216 --> 00:20:36.178
What do you say, sewer plum?
Want to give it another go?

00:20:36.261 --> 00:20:40.307
Well, I am still in my wedding dress.
And we still have a cake.

00:20:40.390 --> 00:20:41.975
Uh... Half a cake.

00:20:43.477 --> 00:20:46.146
Very well. Morris, Munda,

00:20:46.229 --> 00:20:48.982
I now pronounce you man and wife.

00:20:49.066 --> 00:20:50.525
May I kiss the bride?

00:20:51.777 --> 00:20:53.528
Congratulations.